"""
Generate libos/freebsd's kernel interface headers from a FreeBSD source
tree.

Nothing built for FreeBSD runs here, so values are read at compile
time: each constant, size or offset becomes the operand of an inline
'.ascii' directive in a C file that includes the kernel headers, the
file is compiled to assembly for the FreeBSD target, and the values are
read back from the assembly. Structures are emitted as the members
picolibc uses at the kernel's offsets with byte padding between, so no
FreeBSD header text is copied.

usage: make-freebsd-headers --sys <freebsd>/sys --out libos/freebsd [--arch x86_64]
"""

